eza
------------------------------------------
eza is a modern alternative for the venerable file-listing command-line program
ls that ships with Unix and Linux operating systems, giving it more features
and better defaults. It uses colours to distinguish file types and metadata. It
knows about symlinks, extended attributes, and Git. And it's small, fast, and
just one single binary.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cargo-1.91.0-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/eza-community/eza

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/eza-community/eza/archive/refs/tags/v0.23.5.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack eza-0.23.5-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./eza-0.23.5-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/eza-0.23.5-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/eza-0.23.5-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(eza)
  /usr/bin/eza.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/eza.README
  /usr/share/doc/eza/LICENSE.txt
  /usr/share/doc/eza/README.md

